The '''2016 FIFA Club World Cup final''' was the final match of the [[2016 FIFA Club World Cup]], an [[association football]] tournament hosted by [[Japan]]. It was the 13th final of the [[FIFA Club World Cup]], a [[FIFA]]-organised tournament between the winners of the six continental confederations, as well as the host nation's league champions.

The final was contested between Spanish club [[Real Madrid CF|Real Madrid]], representing [[UEFA]] as the reigning champions of the [[UEFA Champions League]], and Japanese club [[Kashima Antlers]], representing the host country as the reigning champions of the [[J1 League]]. It was the first time a team from Asia played in the final. The match was played at the [[International Stadium Yokohama]] in [[Yokohama]] on 18 December 2016.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://resources.fifa.com/mm/document/tournament/competition/02/81/20/44/fcwc2016_matchschedule_newformat_04122016_neutral.pdf |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161213043223/http://resources.fifa.com/mm/document/tournament/competition/02/81/20/44/fcwc2016_matchschedule_newformat_04122016_neutral.pdf |url-status=dead |archive-date=December 13, 2016 |title=Match Schedule – FIFA Club World Cup Japan 2016 |website=FIFA.com |publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association |date=15 July 2016 |access-date=15 July 2016}}</ref>

Real Madrid won the match 4–2 after [[Overtime (sports)#Association football|extra time]] to claim their 2nd title.<ref name="match summary">{{cite news |url=https://www.fifa.com/clubworldcup/matches/round=276112/match=300364984/match-report.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161220125922/http://www.fifa.com/clubworldcup/matches/round=276112/match=300364984/match-report.html |url-status=dead |archive-date=December 20, 2016 |title=Ronaldo hat-trick sees off spirited Kashima |website=FIFA.com |publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association |date=18 December 2016 |access-date=18 December 2016}}</ref>

==Background==
Kashima Antlers became the first Asian club to reach the FIFA Club World Cup final.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/38318258 |title=Atletico Nacional 0 Kashima Antlers 3 |website=[[BBC Sport]] |publisher=British Broadcasting Corporation |date=14 December 2016 |access-date=15 December 2016}}</ref> It was also the first time that an Asian club won against a South American side in the history of the competition, and the third time that South American champions failed to qualify for the final, after the [[2010 FIFA Club World Cup|2010]] and [[2013 FIFA Club World Cup|2013]] editions.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2016/dec/14/kashima-antlers-beat-atletico-nacional-reach-club-world-cup-final |title=Kashima Antlers beat Atlético Nacional to reach Club World Cup final |website=[[theguardian.com]] |publisher=The Guardian |date=14 December 2016 |access-date=15 December 2016}}</ref>

For Real Madrid, the match was their second final, after having won the [[2014 FIFA Club World Cup Final|2014 final]].<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.fifa.com/clubworldcup/matches/round=276112/match=300364984/preview.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161218131632/http://www.fifa.com/clubworldcup/matches/round=276112/match=300364984/preview.html |url-status=dead |archive-date=December 18, 2016 |title=Favourites face surprise package in Yokohama |website=FIFA.com |publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association |date=16 December 2016 |access-date=16 December 2016}}</ref> This was the 12th time in 13 tournaments in which a European team made it to the final.

