===Real Madrid===
Real Madrid entered the competition in the semi-finals, facing Mexican side and [[2015–16 CONCACAF Champions League|CONCACAF Champions League]] winners [[Club América|América]]. [[Karim Benzema]] opened the scoring for Real in first half stoppage time, putting them ahead at the break. [[Cristiano Ronaldo]] secured the 2–0 victory and final spot for ''Los Blancos'' with a goal in second half stoppage time.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.fifa.com/clubworldcup/matches/round=276110/match=300364982/match-report.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161216162358/http://www.fifa.com/clubworldcup/matches/round=276110/match=300364982/match-report.html |url-status=dead |archive-date=December 16, 2016 |title=Real overcome America to reach final |website=FIFA.com |publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association |date=15 December 2016 |access-date=18 December 2016}}</ref>

===Kashima Antlers===
Kashima Antlers started the tournament in the quarter-final play-off, facing New Zealand side [[Auckland City FC|Auckland City]], winners of the [[2016 OFC Champions League|OFC Champions League]]. Auckland opened the scoring via a goal from [[Kim Dae-wook]] in the 50th minute. Seventeen minutes later, [[Shuhei Akasaki]] equalised for the hosts. With two minutes remaining, [[Mu Kanazaki]] grabbed the late winner, sending Kashima through to the quarter-finals with a 2–1 win.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.fifa.com/clubworldcup/matches/round=276106/match=300364978/match-report.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161208214543/http://www.fifa.com/clubworldcup/matches/round=276106/match=300364978/match-report.html |url-status=dead |archive-date=December 8, 2016 |title=Kashima Antlers fight back to overcome Auckland |website=FIFA.com |publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association |date=8 December 2016 |access-date=18 December 2016}}</ref>

In the quarter-finals, ''the Antlers'' faced the [[2016 CAF Champions League|CAF Champions League]] winners and South African champions [[Mamelodi Sundowns F.C.|Mamelodi Sundowns]]. [[Yasushi Endo]] opened the scoring in the 63rd minute to put Kashima ahead, before Shuhei Akasaki once again scored with two minutes remaining to secure the 2–0 win and semi-final spot.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.fifa.com/clubworldcup/matches/round=276104/match=300364977/match-report.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161212124943/http://www.fifa.com/clubworldcup/matches/round=276104/match=300364977/match-report.html |url-status=dead |archive-date=December 12, 2016 |title=Endo, Mu sink Sundowns |website=FIFA.com |publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association |date=11 December 2016 |access-date=18 December 2016}}</ref>

In the semi-finals, Kashima met the [[2016 Copa Libertadores|Copa Libertadores]] winners, [[Atlético Nacional]] of Colombia. In the 33rd minute, Hungarian referee [[Viktor Kassai]] awarded a historic penalty to Kashima. This was the first time that the video assistant referee (VAR) system was used to award a penalty in football, following a video replay review by Kassai. The review was initiated after Kassai received information from Dutchman [[Danny Makkelie]] about a missed incident in Atlético Nacional's penalty box.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.fifa.com/clubworldcup/news/y=2016/m=12/news=video-review-used-for-penalty-decision-in-fifa-club-world-cup-japan-20-2860247.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161216131636/http://www.fifa.com/clubworldcup/news/y=2016/m=12/news=video-review-used-for-penalty-decision-in-fifa-club-world-cup-japan-20-2860247.html |url-status=dead |archive-date=December 16, 2016 |title=Video review used for penalty decision in FIFA Club World Cup Japan 2016 semi-final |website=FIFA.com |publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association |date=14 December 2016 |access-date=14 December 2016}}</ref> [[Shoma Doi]] then successfully converted the penalty to put Kashima ahead at the interval. Yasushi Endo extended their lead in the 83rd minute, before [[Yuma Suzuki]] scored two minutes later, wrapping up the 3–0 win for Kashima and sending them through to the final.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.fifa.com/clubworldcup/matches/round=276110/match=300364980/match-report.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161215145815/http://www.fifa.com/clubworldcup/matches/round=276110/match=300364980/match-report.html |url-status=dead |archive-date=December 15, 2016 |title=Antlers down Atletico Nacional to reach final |website=FIFA.com |publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association |date=14 December 2016 |access-date=18 December 2016}}</ref>

==Match==
[[File:Nissan International Stadium Yokohama.jpg|thumb|International Stadium Yokohama (also known as Nissan Stadium) in Yokohama, Japan, hosted the match.]]

===Summary===
Real Madrid centre-forward [[Karim Benzema]] opened the scoring in the ninth minute with a right foot shot from seven yards out after an initial shot from [[Luka Modrić]] was saved by [[Hitoshi Sogahata]] with the rebound coming straight back to Benzema. [[Gaku Shibasaki]] equalised for Kashima Antlers shortly before the interval with a low left footed shot from six yards out to the right corner of the net. In the 52nd minute, Shibasaki scored his second to put Kashima ahead with a low left foot shot from outside the penalty box that skimmed past Real goalkeeper [[Keylor Navas]] and into the left corner of the net. In the sixtieth minute, Antlers defender [[Shuto Yamamoto]] fouled Real forward [[Lucas Vázquez]] in the box, resulting in a penalty awarded to Madrid.<ref>{{cite web|url= https://www.telegraph.co.uk/football/2016/12/18/real-madrid-vs-kashima-antlers-live-score-goal-updates-club/|title=Real Madrid 4 Kashima Antlers 2: Cristiano Ronaldo hat-trick wins the day but they need extra time to do it |date=18 December 2016|work=Telegraph|access-date=23 February 2017}}</ref> Forward [[Cristiano Ronaldo]] converted the spot kick shooting low to his left to equalise for the European champions. Both sides had additional opportunities to score, but with no further goals in regulation, the match went to extra time.<ref>{{cite web|url= https://www.theguardian.com/football/live/2016/dec/18/real-madrid-v-kashima-antlers-club-world-cup-final-live|title=Real Madrid 4-2 Kashima Antlers: Club World Cup final – as it happened|date=18 December 2016|work=Guardian|access-date=23 February 2017}}</ref>

In the 98th minute, Ronaldo scored his second goal of the match to put Real Madrid ahead once again with a low left-footed shot from inside the penalty box which went under the goalkeeper, following a through ball by Benzema.<ref>{{cite web|url= https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/38338721|title=Real Madrid 4-2 Kashima Antlers|date=18 December 2016|work=BBC Sport|access-date=23 February 2017}}</ref> In the final minute of the first half of extra time, Ronaldo completed his hat-trick for Real Madrid with a left-footed shot from the center of the box into the roof of the net, following a pass from [[Toni Kroos]]. The hat-trick goal sealed the 4–2 win for Real, giving them their second Club World Cup title in three years.<ref name="match summary"/>

